      "created_at": "2016-06-15T15:59:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-06-15T15:59:00Z",
      "body": "I think the set of people who disable usage reporting, and the set of people who either know what RAPPOR is (or will hold off what they're trying to do for long enough to educate themselves) is pretty small.\n\nAlso, \n\n> This is also prejudicial since the kind of people that deactivate usage reporting are possibly correlated to the kind of people that say, use a specific other feature, so you cannot simply extrapolate from the usage reports you have.\n\nAppears to contradict \n\n> No one can say if the reported value is actually true (and if the client does use an outdated and potentially vulnerable version!), but that's not relevant since what you are looking for is trends.\n\nSince you don't gain the ability to extrapolate from the usage reports by using RAPPOR, as I understand you.\n",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
